(Software Requirements Specification \(SRS\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(1.1 Purpose and scope) Tj
T*
(This specification defines the passenger reservation and railway administration workflows delivered) Tj
T*
(by the React, Django REST Framework and MySQL application. The project uses simulated payments and) Tj
T*
(queued notifications; it does not transfer real money or deliver SMS/email through a provider.) Tj
T*
(1.2 Audience and definitions) Tj
T*
(Audience: passengers, administrators, developers, testers and evaluators. PNR = Passenger Name) Tj
T*
(Record; API = Application Programming Interface; CSRF = Cross-Site Request Forgery; RBAC =) Tj
T*
(Role-Based Access Control; RTM = Requirements Traceability Matrix; NFR = Non-Functional Requirement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Overall description) Tj
T*
(The browser frontend calls Django API endpoints, whose feature services use parameterized SQL) Tj
T*
(against an InnoDB MySQL database. Passengers authenticate and manage their own reservations.) Tj
T*
(Administrators manage railway data and view operational records. External payment and notification) Tj
T*
(providers are outside the current implementation.) Tj
T*
(Dependencies: Python 3.10+, Node.js 20+, MySQL 8.0.16+, configured environment and schema. A real) Tj
T*
(MySQL integration deployment is not validated by mocked unit tests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. External interfaces) Tj
T*
(- Passenger and admin web interfaces: React/Vite.) Tj
T*
(- JSON HTTP API: Django REST Framework under /api.) Tj
T*
(- Persistent store: MySQL via mysql-connector-python; schema is in database/schema.sql.) Tj
T*
(- Security: session cookies, CSRF tokens, role checks, password hashing, HTTPS required for) Tj
T*
(production.) Tj
T*
(- External services: payment is simulated; notification and refund records are persisted but) Tj
T*
(provider delivery/settlement is not included.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Functional requirements) Tj
T*
(Each FR is stated as a testable behavior. IDs are stable for the accompanying test plan.) Tj
T*
(|  ID  |  Priority  |  Requirement  |  Acceptance evidence  |) Tj
T*
(| --- | --- | --- | --- |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-001  |  High  |  Register a passenger with validated inputs and hashed password.  |  Valid) Tj
T*
(registration succeeds; invalid/duplicate data is rejected.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-002  |  High  |  Authenticate an active passenger and end the session on logout.  | ) Tj
T*
(Login/logout and unauthorized access tests.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-003  |  High  |  Authenticate an active administrator separately from passengers.  | ) Tj
T*
(Passenger cannot access admin endpoints.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-004  |  High  |  Return selectable stations and travel classes.  |  Catalog endpoints) Tj
T*
(return valid options.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-005  |  High  |  Search train schedules by origin, destination and journey date.  | ) Tj
T*
(Matching routes returned; invalid queries rejected.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-006  |  High  |  Show available seats for a selected schedule and class.  |  Confirmed and) Tj
T*
(unexpired held allocations are excluded.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-007  |  High  |  Collect and validate passenger details for a booking.  |  Missing/invalid) Tj
T*
(traveler data rejected.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-008  |  High  |  Calculate and preserve a fare snapshot for a reservation.  |  Fare) Tj
T*
(returned and persisted consistently.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-009  |  High  |  Create a booking with a unique PNR and temporary seat holds.  |  Booking,) Tj
T*
(travelers and holds commit atomically.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-010  |  High  |  Prevent duplicate bookings from request retries and overlapping seat) Tj
T*
(allocation.  |  Idempotency and inventory-lock tests pass.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-011  |  High  |  Confirm an eligible held booking using simulated payment.  |  Booking and) Tj
T*
(seat statuses become CONFIRMED together.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-012  |  High  |  Display passenger booking history and PNR status.  |  Only bookings owned) Tj
T*
(by signed-in user appear.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-013  |  High  |  Cancel an eligible booking and release its seats.  |  Booking, allocations) Tj
T*
(and cancellation rows update together.  |) Tj
T*
ET
