(|  RRS-F-014  |  High  |  Calculate cancellation charges and persist pending refunds.  | ) Tj
T*
(Passenger-level cancellation/refund rows exist.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-015  |  Medium  |  Queue booking notification records when confirmed.  |  Email/SMS queue) Tj
T*
(rows are created where applicable; no delivery claim.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-016  |  High  |  Let administrators create, edit, deactivate or safely remove trains.  | ) Tj
T*
(Role checks and dependency-preserving removal tests.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-017  |  High  |  Let administrators manage stations, routes and train-route assignments.  |) Tj
T*
(Validation and dependency checks prevent invalid updates.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-018  |  High  |  Let administrators manage schedules and seat inventory.  |  Existing) Tj
T*
(bookings are protected from unsafe changes.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-019  |  Medium  |  Let administrators inspect bookings, cancellations and refunds.  | ) Tj
T*
(Protected detail and search endpoints return scoped records.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-F-020  |  Medium  |  Expose application and database health endpoints.  |  API health and) Tj
T*
(database outage/recovery tests.  |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Non-functional requirements) Tj
T*
(These are evaluation targets, not assertions that production metrics have been measured.) Tj
T*
(|  ID  |  Category  |  Measurable requirement / verification  |) Tj
T*
(| --- | --- | --- |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-NF-001  |  Performance  |  Train search P95 latency at or below 3 seconds under a documented) Tj
T*
(representative load; run scripts/benchmark_train_search.py against a test MySQL database.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-NF-002  |  Availability  |  Target 99.5% monthly availability excluding announced) Tj
T*
(maintenance; verify with operational uptime measurements \(not yet established\).  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-NF-003  |  Reliability  |  Booking, payment and cancellation multi-row changes are atomic;) Tj
T*
(inject failures and verify rollback and idempotent retries.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-NF-004  |  Compatibility  |  Main screens render in Chrome, Firefox, Edge and Safari; execute) Tj
T*
(Playwright browser suite and record results.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-NF-005  |  Maintainability  |  Backend unit suite, Python compilation and frontend build) Tj
T*
(complete successfully on every reviewed PR; inspect GitHub Actions logs.  |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.1 Security objectives) Tj
T*
(- SO-01: Prevent unauthorized access to passenger reservations and administrative operations.) Tj
T*
(- SO-02: Protect credentials and transactional integrity against disclosure, forgery and concurrent) Tj
T*
(updates.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5.2 Security requirements) Tj
T*
(|  ID  |  Requirement  |  Acceptance test  |) Tj
T*
(| --- | --- | --- |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-SR-001  |  Store passwords using a one-way password hash; never return hashes in API) Tj
T*
(responses.  |  Registration/authentication tests and response inspection.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-SR-002  |  Require an authenticated session and enforce passenger ownership/admin RBAC.  | ) Tj
T*
(Unauthorized and cross-user endpoint tests.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-SR-003  |  Enforce CSRF checks on state-changing browser requests.  |  Missing/invalid CSRF) Tj
T*
(token tests.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-SR-004  |  Use parameterized SQL and validate IDs and request fields.  |  Input validation) Tj
T*
(and source review.  |) Tj
T*
(|  RRS-SR-005  |  Use secure cookies and HTTPS for production; never commit secrets.  | ) Tj
T*
(Configuration review of production deployment.  |) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Quality attributes and acceptance) Tj
T*
(High-priority FRs must be demonstrated, security tests must pass, critical defects must be resolved,) Tj
T*
(and the RTM must identify execution evidence. Tests with mocked database access are not substitutes) Tj
T*
(for real database integration testing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. UML use-case diagrams) Tj
T*
